* RSpice op-amp macromodels (single-pole, ideal input offset of 0 V).
* X1 inp inn out opamp  → A0 = 1e5, pole at ~10 Hz, Rout = 50 Ω.

.subckt opamp inp inn out
Rin inp inn 1meg
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1
R1 n1 0 1
C1 n1 0 15.9m
E1 out 0 n1 0 1e5
Rout out 0 50
.ends opamp

* Unity-gain-stable variant with a lower pole and 75 Ω output.
.subckt opamp_u inp inn out
Rin inp inn 10meg
G1 0 n1 inp inn 1
R1 n1 0 1
C1 n1 0 31.8m
E1 out 0 n1 0 2e5
Rout out 0 75
.ends opamp_u

* Comparator: high gain, no compensation.
.subckt comparator inp inn out PARAMS: gain=1e6 rout=100
Rin inp inn 1meg
E1 out 0 inp inn {gain}
Rout out 0 {rout}
.ends comparator
